<title>POLAND: POLAND SEEN MAINTAINING HIGH WAGE GROWTH - REPORT.</title>
<headline>POLAND SEEN MAINTAINING HIGH WAGE GROWTH - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland is likely to maintain its rapid wage growth, already higher than envisaged in the 1997 budget, Government Centre for Strategic Studies (CSS) said in a report on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The report said real wage growth in the enterprise sector was at 4.1 percent in January-April period, against 2.5-percent growth envisaged in the budget for the whole 1997.</p>
<p>It said average wage in the enterprise sector was likely to rise to 1,150 zlotys in 1997, 4.5 percent higher than last year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
